<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Godfrey Huggins</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1883–1971</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lord Malvern, Godfrey Huggins, 1st Viscount Malvern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Godfrey Huggins was an English-born surgeon who became prime minister of Southern Rhodesia from 1933 to 1953, the longest tenure in the Commonwealth. He oversaw growth based on tobacco, mining and white immigration and pressed for union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-rhodesia">Northern Rhodesia</a> and Nyasaland. He became the first prime minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federation-of-rhodesia-and-nyasaland">Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland</a> in 1953.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/godfrey-huggins.jpg" alt="Godfrey Huggins" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Codexbox1 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Godfrey_Huggins_in_1936.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
